8. Vendor-derived content

   This project is not affiliated with or endorsed by FNIRSI. FNIRSI and the product names are
   trademarks of their owners. The bootloader port in `bootloader/` is written from the
   disassembly of the vendor's bootloader and is derived from it; its three larger data blocks
   (font bitmaps, a table, the packed initial RAM image) are not included and are extracted from
   your own meter's flash (`make vendor-data`). The application port in `firmware/` is written
   from the disassembly of the vendor's application V1.1 and is derived from it; its larger data
   blocks (fonts, pictures, tables, the packed initial RAM image; listed in
   `firmware/vendor_blobs.tsv`) are not included and are extracted from your own copy of the
   vendor's update file (`make vendor-data`). The rest of the repository contains no code or
   data derived from the vendor's firmware; it names vendor addresses as facts about the meter and
   does not include the vendor application or bootloader images. No license for vendor-derived
   content is granted here; its use is at your own responsibility.
